@startuml UC-A5-view-my-name-and-role-design-sequence
!include ../../domain/diagrams/_style.puml
hide footbox
title UC-A5 View my name and role (design sequence)
' Design level (decision 9): the routes, use cases, ports and adapters that do the work. The analysis level is UC-A5-view-my-name-and-role-analysis-sequence.puml.
' Built today: the dashboard, GET /me, the token check, the 403 route guard and AccessService.account_for. The page is the
' dashboard (there is no profile page). The 403 is a route guard, not a domain rule.
' Step ids are the main flow numbers of UC-A5. The token refresh (UC-A6) is not drawn.
' Evolved from MK3 UC-A4: /me now joins Keycloak's facts and our own in one answer.

actor "Person" as P
participant "Web server" as W #E6F0FB
participant "API\n/me" as A #E6F0FB
participant "AccessService" as S #E7F4EA
database "API database" as D #ECECEC

P -> W : 1 open dashboard
W -> A : 2 GET /me + access token
A -> A : 3 verify the token
alt not valid
  A --> W : 401
else
  A -> S : 4 account_for(identity, name, email)
  S -> D : 4 find by identity
  D --> S : account (role, status)
  S -> D : 4 save if name or email changed
  alt deactivated
    A --> W : 5 403 account deactivated
  else pending or active
    A --> W : 6 name, email, role, status
    W --> P : 7 show name and role
  end
end
@enduml
